      "latin": "clāmō, clāmāre, clāmāvī, clāmātum",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "shout, cry out",
      "grammar": "verb, first conjugation; intransitive, or with what is shouted",
      "evidence": [
        "Plaut. Men. 1114b: <span lang=\"la\">Quid clāmās? quīn tacēs?</span>",
        "Ter. Ad. 728: <span lang=\"la\">Nōn clāmās? nōn īnsānīs?</span>",
        "Traupman 299"
      ],
      "comment": "The everyday word, of people, and in comedy even of snoring; also of geese and crickets (Lewis &amp; Short). With an object it is to call out something, or call on someone: <span lang=\"la\">clāmāre aliquem</span>."
    },
    {
      "latin": "clāmor, clāmōris m.",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "a shout, shouting",
      "evidence": [
        "Plaut. Bacch. 874: <span lang=\"la\">ut nē clāmōrem hīc faciās</span>"
      ],
      "comment": "A shout or the noise of shouting: <span lang=\"la\">clāmōrem facere</span>, to shout, make a row."
    },
    {
      "latin": "exclāmō, exclāmāre, exclāmāvī, exclāmātum",
      "status": "alternative",
